>>
Rule 1 (tensor rank must be non-negative)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 0
>>
Rule 2 (each dimension size is non-negative if any dimensions exist)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) > 0 then ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) ≥ 0
>>
Rule 3 (min/max are well-ordered for scalar or non-empty tensors)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = 0 ∨ (ndim(v_1) > 0 ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > 0) then min(v_1) ≤ max(v_1)
>>
Rule 4 (scalar tensor has identical min and max)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = 0 then min(v_1) = max(v_1)
>>
Rule 5 (last dimension size is non-negative when rank > 0)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) > 0 then shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 1) ≥ 0
>>
Rule 6 (dtype of the input tensor is well-defined)
{v_1 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) = dtype_(v_1)
